    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ede8124b_05788cf6",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-17T20:48:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per latest BAP specification, all parameters above are defined as generic fields, not specific to LC3 codec. Other codecs in future have freedom to choose which ones they want to use.\nI don\u0027t have strong opinion wether to keep these field in Lc3Parameters, or have them defined in LeAudioCodecCapabilities and LeAudioCodecConfiguration.\nIf you have any good reason I can move them.\n\n\nI moved audioChannelAllocation and audioChannelCount to more proper place.",
      "parentUuid": "42c86729_791ed255",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bed08e00b59d8f825899df87aa40cd67a56ff713",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e29ed302_74f7219b",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1318371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-18T07:37:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, so is it used in current LE Audio or just some concept that can be used in the future? I just think that it is more clear if all generic fields are grouped together and all parameters here are specific to codec.",
      "parentUuid": "ede8124b_05788cf6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bed08e00b59d8f825899df87aa40cd67a56ff713",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "879512eb_8328b37e",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-18T10:19:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All fields are defined as generic LTV (length-type-value). I.e. there is generic \"frame duration\".\n\nLC3 integration requirements list LTV fields that MUST be specified for LC3 codec parameters - these are all listed here, and they are all generic.\n\nIn future there might be codec that either reuses those LTV definitions, or make new ones that it needs.\n\nThere is no group of fields that\u0027s defined as \"must have\" for possible future codecs, so I would prefer to not create a generic fields group.",
      "parentUuid": "e29ed302_74f7219b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bed08e00b59d8f825899df87aa40cd67a56ff713",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
